{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\nThe op-cert service owns per-job boto3/SSM/region lookup and patches process-global key/principal/push state. That couples app config to one deployment secret store, lets jobs observe different keys in one process, and creates concurrency/cleanup hazards. ADR 0098 retains SSM as a deployment storage option but moves application binding to startup.\n## Outcome\nAt startup accept exactly one of preferred `REBAR_OPCERT_KEY_PATH` or compat `REBAR_OPCERT_PRIVATE_KEY`. Validate before queue/worker/network/workspace creation, copy into a process-owned 0700 dir/0600 file, build one immutable signer/runtime, and pass signer/principal/push policy context-locally to jobs. The process never rereads/reloads; restart observes replacement. Remove application-runtime SSM/boto3/region coupling and per-job retrieval.\n## Plan\n1. Replace `opcert_service.ssm`/per-job key acquisition with startup composition in config/key-provider/app. Reject missing, both-set, unreadable, non-regular, malformed, encrypted/passphrase, or non-Ed25519 input before service work. The path source (`REBAR_OPCERT_KEY_PATH`) also requires a regular-file 0600-or-stricter check; the inline value source (`REBAR_OPCERT_PRIVATE_KEY`) has no on-disk mode. Both are copied to the process-owned 0700/0600 runtime location, mode-checked after copy.\n2. Copy key bytes to a new process-owned runtime directory/file at 0700/0600; never modify/delete the deployment source. Cleanup removes only Rebar's copy on graceful shutdown. Deployment tmpfs/restart owns crash cleanup.\n3. Replace global environment/state patching with a typed context-local signer, environment principal, and push policy passed through jobs/workspace/signing. Concurrent and timed-out workers cannot observe or mutate one another's context.\n4. **Thread the immutable signer through the out-of-`opcert_service/` producer seam.** The key/principal are resolved from `os.environ` in `src/rebar/_opcert_signing.py` — `ensure_opcert_key` (`REBAR_OPCERT_KEY_PATH`, ~line 169), `opcert_principal` (`REBAR_OPCERT_ENV_ID`, ~line 193), and callers `mint_opcert_record`/`sign_opcert_manifest`, via the intermediary `rebar.signing.sign_manifest` (`signing.py:529-567`, the sole caller of `mint_opcert_record` on the completion path) — reached from the service via `src/rebar/_commands/transition_close.py:sign_completion_verdict` (called from `opcert_service/jobs.py`). Convert these (including `sign_manifest`, which must accept and forward the binding) to take an explicit signer-key-handle + principal (optional `OpcertSigner` binding); the service passes the startup-bound context-local signer, so removing `keyprov.py`'s `os.environ` patching cannot silently break signing. The developer-local close-gate caller (non-service `rebar transition ... closed` and `review-plan`'s signing) passes no binding and keeps the existing env/genesis default. Also route the push-policy read-site (`_push_mode`/`REBAR_SYNC_PUSH`) to the context-local push policy when a binding is present, env default otherwise.\n5. Decouple the op-cert APPLICATION runtime from SSM/region: remove `REBAR_OPCERT_SSM_KEY_PARAM` and the key-retrieval `AWS_REGION`/`AWS_DEFAULT_REGION` from the opcert service env in `infra/compose/docker-compose.yml`, drop the app runtime boto3 need in `infra/compose/Dockerfile.opcert`, and materialize ADR 0049's SSM value into the process file/value startup contract BEFORE the app starts, OUTSIDE the application (`infra/scripts/fetch-secrets.sh`). ACCURACY: there is no opcert 'app role' and no key IAM in `opcert.tf` ('NO new IAM here'); SSM read is the shared `/rebar/prod/*` grant `aws_iam_role_policy.ssm_params_read` (`rebar-gerrit-ssm-params-read`) on the shared `gerrit_instance` INSTANCE role in `infra/terraform/iam.tf`, co-used by the still-required origin-guard + gerrit secrets — so it is NOT dropped. Decoupling is at the application-runtime boundary (container env/deps + materialize-before-startup), not by removing shared IAM.\n6. Preserve ADR 0049's Ed25519/DSSE algorithm, trust roots/eras, producer, authoritative fetch, envelope persistence, guard, and no-workspace-push invariants.\n\n\n## Testing (RED -> GREEN)\n- Startup component tests instrument queue, worker, network, and workspace factories and assert every invalid source fails before all four.\n- Filesystem tests assert source untouched, process directory 0700, copy 0600, stable bytes after source replacement, restart observes new bytes, graceful cleanup removes only copy, and stale tmpfs clears in container restart canary.\n- **Signer-seam tests** assert the signing seam (`sign_completion_verdict`/`mint_opcert_record`/`ensure_opcert_key`/`opcert_principal`) signs from the passed context-local binding (not `os.environ`) when the service supplies one — proven by signing with a distinct injected key while `REBAR_OPCERT_KEY_PATH`/`REBAR_OPCERT_ENV_ID` are unset — and with no binding still resolves via env/genesis as before (regression pin).\n- Concurrent/timed-out job tests use distinct principals/policies and prove context isolation, immutable startup signer, existing producer signatures, and no workspace push remote.\n- Structural tests assert `src/rebar/opcert_service` has no boto3/SSM/region import or runtime parameter after cutover; deployment assertions retain optional SSM-at-rest materialization outside the application and assert the opcert compose service env carries no `REBAR_OPCERT_SSM_KEY_PARAM`/key-retrieval region and the image needs no runtime boto3 (the shared instance-role SSM grant in iam.tf is intentionally untouched).\n- [operator-attested] Hosted op-cert/review-bot signing canary records deployment/run ids, source kind (never value/path), signature verification, restart result, modes, timestamp, and redacted failure outcome.\n\n## Compatibility / rollback\nExpand deployment input first while the legacy per-job facade exists; before removal rollback selects the legacy facade, after removal rollback requires the same startup source contract (signatures/envelopes stay compatible). The signer-seam parameter is additive/optional, so the developer-local close path is unaffected. Inline multiline env input stays a documented weaker compat source, removed from unrelated children.\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Exactly-one source validation rejects every named invalid case before queue, worker, network, or workspace construction.\n- [ ] The process-owned copy is 0700/0600, stable for process lifetime, observes replacement only after restart, and cleanup never alters the deployment source.\n- [ ] Concurrent and timed-out jobs prove context-local signer/principal/push isolation, one immutable startup signer, existing signature verification, and no workspace push remote.\n- [ ] The out-of-`opcert_service/` signing seam (`_opcert_signing.py`, `signing.py:sign_manifest`, `transition_close.py:sign_completion_verdict`) signs from the injected context-local binding when the service supplies one, and the developer-local close path retains its prior env/genesis resolution unchanged (regression pinned).\n- [ ] The op-cert application runtime (the `src/rebar/opcert_service` process/container) has no SSM/boto3/region/key-parameter dependency: the compose service carries no `REBAR_OPCERT_SSM_KEY_PARAM`/key-retrieval region and the image needs no runtime boto3; the key is materialized to the startup contract before start. The shared `/rebar/prod/*` instance-role SSM grant in `iam.tf` is deliberately UNCHANGED (co-used by origin-guard/gerrit secrets, not an app-role).\n- [ ] Secret/key sentinels are absent from repr, serialization, argv, logs, exceptions, output, fingerprints, provenance, children, and persisted envelopes beyond the existing public signature.\n- [ ] [operator-attested] Hosted signing/restart/tmpfs canaries pass with the required redacted evidence recorded."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1787027592174706001,"uuid":"a8aa831a-64b2-4a98-8c98-e6e911730e28"}